# Core VFS Refactor

Foundational refactor required before Q-LINK can be implemented.

## Goal
Abstract all std::fs calls behind a FileSystemProvider trait to enable virtual file systems.

## Implementation

\`\`\`rust
pub trait FileSystemProvider: Send + Sync {
    fn read_dir(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<Vec<DirEntry>>;
    fn read_file(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<Vec<u8>>;
    fn write_file(&self, path: &Path, content: &[u8]) -> Result<()>;
    fn metadata(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<Metadata>;
    fn exists(&self, path: &Path) -> bool;
    fn is_dir(&self, path: &Path) -> bool;
    fn create_dir(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<()>;
    fn remove_file(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<()>;
    fn remove_dir(&self, path: &Path) -> Result<()>;
    fn rename(&self, from: &Path, to: &Path) -> Result<()>;
    fn copy(&self, from: &Path, to: &Path) -> Result<()>;
}
\`\`\`

## Steps
1. Define trait in new src/vfs/mod.rs
2. Implement LocalFS wrapping std::fs
3. Refactor file_ops.rs to use trait
4. Refactor App to hold Arc<dyn FileSystemProvider>
5. Update all plugins that do file I/O
6. Add tests for LocalFS implementation

## Files to modify
- src/file_ops.rs (heavy changes)
- src/app/mod.rs
- src/plugins/* (any that use std::fs directly)

Use inventory or linkme crate for automatic plugin registration.

Options:
1. inventory crate - distributed slice pattern
2. linkme crate - similar but different implementation
3. ctor crate - constructor functions

Pattern:
```rust
// In each plugin crate
inventory::submit! {
    PluginRegistration::new(|| Box::new(GitPlugin::new()))
}

// In main app
for registration in inventory::iter::<PluginRegistration> {
    plugin_manager.register(registration.create());
}
```

This eliminates the 40+ manual register() calls in app/mod.rs.

Create a reusable table widget in src/ui/components/table.rs

Features:
- Column specification (name, width, alignment)
- Header row with blue styling
- Row rendering with proper column alignment
- Selection highlighting for rows
- Automatic column width calculation option

API:
```rust
pub struct Column {
    pub name: String,
    pub width: usize,
    pub align: Align, // Left, Right, Center
}

pub struct Table {
    columns: Vec<Column>,
}

impl Table {
    pub fn render_header(&self, frame, area, colors);
    pub fn render_row(&self, frame, y, values: &[String], style);
}
```

Used by: git config, beads list, proc views
